# Sunshine Ledger — scheduled-job monitoring configuration.
#
# Copy to `monitoring.env` beside this file and fill in the push URLs.
# Without it, or with the values left empty, the jobs run exactly as they
# do now and every ping is a silent no-op.
#
# TO SET UP (Uptime Kuma, already running on this host):
#
#   1. Add New Monitor -> Monitor Type: "Push"
#   2. Friendly Name:   Sunshine Ledger — nightly backup
#      Heartbeat Interval: 86400   (daily; the job runs at 03:00)
#      Retries: 0
#   3. Kuma shows a Push URL ending in a token. Paste it below.
#   4. Repeat for ingestion (runs at 04:00) and paste that URL too.
#
# WHY THE INTERVAL MATTERS: Kuma alerts when a ping does not arrive within
# the heartbeat window. That is what catches the failure a log-based check
# cannot see -- the job not running at all because cron stopped or the host
# is down. Set it a little longer than the real gap between runs so a slow
# night doesn't page you: 86400 for a daily job is the interval itself,
# and Kuma's own grace handling covers normal jitter.
#
# The weekly GDELT run (Sundays 05:00) shares the ingestion monitor. It is
# the same script and the same failure surface, and a separate monitor
# would sit "pending" six days a week for no benefit.

BACKUP_PUSH_URL=""
INGESTION_PUSH_URL=""
